{
  "schema": 1,
  "title": "Native UI upgrade performance and preservation audit",
  "environment": {
    "platform": "Linux-6.18.44-x86_64-with-glibc2.39",
    "python": "3.12.14",
    "pygame_ce": "2.5.8",
    "video_driver": "dummy",
    "audio_driver": "dummy"
  },
  "conclusion": "The crowded world remains around 12 ms per frame with all 160 rivals and 322 actors. The richer Activity view adds about 2.11 ms of mean CPU frame work, measuring 7.29 ms mean and 10.44 ms p95. Every measured world and menu frame sequence retained zero repeated PNG decodes. All original graphics, game data records, server rules, world rendering and movement/network code are preserved.",
  "limits": [
    "These are unprofiled Linux headless CPU frame-preparation measurements, not Windows display FPS or a guarantee for a particular PC.",
    "Two world runs per version and one four-menu run per version provide a regression check. Small differences and isolated high percentiles can reflect shared-host scheduling; no meaningful world-speed improvement is claimed.",
    "Warmup excludes first-visit asset/audio loading. Both versions use equal native resolution, a fixed animation timeline and the same synthetic records. New menu layouts intentionally show different detail and visible row counts."
  ],
  "methodology": [
    "Measured processes ran sequentially while other agents paused testing, hashing and packaging.",
    "World: the same benchmark_client_fps.py against immutable baseline_fps1 and current source; 160 rivals, 322 actors, 64 tamer appearances and 128 lead species; original Dawn Sector 004 art; 2048x1152 physical pixels, UI scale 4/3 and zoom 1.5; 960 warmup and 360 measured frames; 10 Hz synthetic snapshots and 60 Hz simulation.",
    "Menus: identical server_fixture/select_view records from preview_ui_screens.py. Each selected project client is imported before the shared fixture; the actual module paths are recorded. Four fresh App instances each receive 240 warmup and 360 measured frames at 2048x1152 pixels and UI scale 4/3.",
    "Menu timing includes event pumping, App.update, WorldRenderer.update and App.draw. Fixture construction, App startup and warmup are excluded. Network polling is disabled for equal preloaded data, and temporary settings isolate player preferences. Real scene-music selection runs through SDL dummy audio.",
    "World summaries are medians of the two per-run statistics, not pooled frame-time percentiles. Raw results retain every run.",
    "Identical PNG-load wrappers were used in both versions. Assertions passed for zero measured PNG loads, zero asset errors, equal world actor counts and native dimensions.",
    "Preservation compares SHA-256 for every original file, excluding interpreter/test caches and .git. Original tree hashes concatenate sorted relative paths, NUL, hexadecimal SHA-256, and newline. Asset-manifest extension is checked record by record: all 21,149 original records remain identical and 199 UI records were added."
  ],
  "commands": {
    "world_baseline": "python tools/benchmark_client_fps.py --project ../baseline_fps1 --bots 160 --warmup 960 --frames 360 --size 2048x1152 --ui-scale 1.3333333333333333 --zoom 1.5 --json world_baseline.json",
    "world_current": "python tools/benchmark_client_fps.py --project . --bots 160 --warmup 960 --frames 360 --size 2048x1152 --ui-scale 1.3333333333333333 --zoom 1.5 --json world_current.json",
    "menus_baseline": "python tools/benchmark_ui_fps.py --project ../baseline_fps1 --warmup 240 --frames 360 --size 2048x1152 --ui-scale 1.3333333333333333 --json menus_baseline.json",
    "menus_current": "python tools/benchmark_ui_fps.py --project . --warmup 240 --frames 360 --size 2048x1152 --ui-scale 1.3333333333333333 --json menus_current.json",
    "order": "World baseline/current pair repeated twice, then menus baseline/current pair; no concurrent workloads."
  },
